{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:07:43.295703Z","id":"7b5c5fd02200e74ac2224fc033f85d93517f02ed07fe0c118d991bf0277308eb","body":{"detail":"main.ts appends tokens.css as a <style> element, and vite.overlay.config.ts compiles the components with css: \"injected\", which Svelte also adds as <style> elements in the shadow root. A deployer page with Content-Security-Policy style-src 'self' (no 'unsafe-inline', no nonce) blocks both: the launcher, composer and list render unstyled. The clip (bridge/src/clip.ts, modern-screenshot) also loads a data:/blob: image, which an img-src without data:/blob: refuses; the report then files with the clip's error. Not covered by any test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"372e1f53a6fbeb164e64ed4322735460fe1d25c4f06b198471ddf8a368f045eb"},"suggested_fix":"Adopt the CSS as a constructed stylesheet (new CSSStyleSheet().replaceSync; root.adoptedStyleSheets), compiling the components with css: \"external\" and inlining the emitted CSS into the bundle; add a CSP case with style-src 'self' to web/e2e/queues.spec.ts.","summary":"The overlay's styles are <style> elements in its shadow root, which a page whose CSP style-src lacks 'unsafe-inline' refuses","tags":["csp","overlay","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:07:43.295779Z","id":"190a6f5dae8aa08534e480442968a7704eb4d175a44fc2e362992b96e36e34c8","body":{"detail":"The poll calls client.myReports() without a cursor and replaces the list with page.reports. A reporter with more reports than the server's page size never sees the older ones, and a reply on one of them does not show.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":134},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"71df012d61085aecd4487f7d2c674fb173dd7c961f5250e67cf8684ce38882c7"},"suggested_fix":"Follow next on demand (a Show more button at the list's end), keeping the polled first page merged with the loaded tail by report ID.","summary":"Your reports shows only the first page of myReports; the cursor (next) is never followed","tags":["overlay","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:07:43.295808Z","id":"127bf81715ef8f5d14c554208c1c67349f64c35523a99462db5f8bcedd94e622","body":{"detail":"The overlay runs in the page's own world (unlike the extension's, web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts, which uses closed roots and an extension-page composer). It is open so Playwright can reach it in web/e2e. The page is the deployer's own, which already holds the reporter's session and the auth callback, and the reporter's Ed25519 key is non-extractable (web/sdk/src/sign.ts), so a closed root would add little; a third-party script on that page can read typed text either way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"2506fc8ee180769cea1d77c3ed518fa3b35075d43268bba807a3dbe05810e5b5"},"summary":"The overlay's shadow root is open, so the page's scripts can read and drive its composer","tags":["overlay","security","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/tokens.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:07:43.295845Z","id":"023befa6be342664a9bbfae23b216a755c182387ab5f2f7a56bb035a15855be4","body":{"detail":"The overlay cannot import theme.css (its :root rules do not apply in a shadow root and would leak into the page), so tokens.css copies the subset it uses onto :host, light and prefers-color-scheme dark. Nothing checks that the two agree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":5},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"6c9d321dacd1af7ce9d71cb3300dcb297fd8a15fe253de184537ad09491788c9"},"suggested_fix":"Generate tokens.css from theme.css at build time (rewriting :root to :host), or add a unit test that compares each token tokens.css sets with theme.css's value.","summary":"tokens.css repeats the shell's colour tokens by hand; a change to web/shell/src/theme.css does not reach the overlay","tags":["overlay","design-tokens","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:46:30.323873Z","id":"d91b4c0f010b9d3ae5520c66c8ec5fac7f78d00921e27c4b6f8ec8568c2fbdd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4355f90f1","summary":"The overlay's host takes HOST_CSS through host.style.cssText and its shadow root adopts one constructed sheet (web/bridge/src/sheet.ts addSheet) of tokens.css and the components' CSS, which web/vite.overlay.config.ts now writes into overlay.js; no <style> is made where adoptedStyleSheets exists. Evidence: web/e2e/deployer-site/server.ts policyFor now sends style-src 'self' 'report-sample'; bazel test //web:e2e_queues PASSED, asserting .launcher has display:flex and the composer border-top-width 3px under that policy, and that the only violation is modern-screenshot's empty font <style>.","supersedes":"7b5c5fd02200e74ac2224fc033f85d93517f02ed07fe0c118d991bf0277308eb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Annotator.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:05:21.880576Z","id":"76dbc4968cbf560b7e2b8dc6d777df37d483ef304c377399d4564e77ecb1bd14","body":{"detail":"web/overlay/src/annotate.ts paint() sizes the plate behind a text mark with ctx.measureText in the PNG sent; the SVG preview in Annotator.svelte guesses sh.text.length * size * 0.56. The plate the reporter sees can be wider or narrower than the one sent, by a few pixels per character for wide or narrow faces.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":101},"content_hash":"89131a7f23f295f05164a39c3a58d8881077799fd81b7babbbdbc408e6c603f8"},"suggested_fix":"Measure the text in the preview with the SVG <text> element's getComputedTextLength() (or an OffscreenCanvas measureText with the same font string) and size the plate from that.","summary":"A text mark's plate in the preview is sized by an estimate (0.56 em per character), not by the canvas's measureText that flatten uses","tags":["overlay","annotate","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/capture.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:05:21.880634Z","id":"46dd589a71d98ba2ce1edada9caf48d1771e921ef6bf0f76c7924fc2574e6ac3","body":{"detail":"Captured.scale for method display is dprOf(win). web/bridge/src/display-capture.ts halves the cropped frame up to 3 times to fit MAX_SIDE and MAX_CLIP_BYTES without saying so, so after a shrink the marks' strokes and text (STROKE_PX and TEXT_PX times scale, web/overlay/src/annotate.ts) are drawn up to 8 times too large for the image.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"77cc99d79f0c9da81f7f5a53c8c223b1fb380bac05238e444e7b1dc11201fe91"},"suggested_fix":"Have DisplayResult carry the scale it drew at (frame px per CSS px after any shrink) and use it here.","summary":"An exact screenshot's scale is taken as the device pixel ratio, though captureDisplay may have shrunk the frame","tags":["overlay","capture","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/capture.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:41:41.383354Z","id":"8703b71ca735d28c24cc53d9ef8b0988399812d98f18904953238a6236853b42","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:eb30655b2","summary":"captureExact now reads the exact screenshot's scale from the PNG's own width over the crop (pngSize), so a frame captureDisplay shrank is measured as it is. web/overlay/src/capture.test.ts 'measures an exact screenshot's scale from its PNG, and places both captures on the page' (300 px PNG of a 200 px crop gives 1.5). bazel test //web:unit PASSED at eb30655b2.","supersedes":"46dd589a71d98ba2ce1edada9caf48d1771e921ef6bf0f76c7924fc2574e6ac3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Annotator.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:41:41.467711Z","id":"b5008076cd6793e0da69f19ca9a9d8bb4649916ed9d17160a36b3d6912701443","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:eb30655b2","summary":"The preview sizes a text mark's plate with annotate.ts textWidth, an OffscreenCanvas measureText in textFont(size), the font paint() draws in; only where there is no OffscreenCanvas is it estimated. bazel test //web:unit //web:typecheck PASSED at eb30655b2.","supersedes":"76dbc4968cbf560b7e2b8dc6d777df37d483ef304c377399d4564e77ecb1bd14","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/ReportView.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:44:36.356887Z","id":"7f5e046fc55547aa0de7612bc8346643a10f0fe51a8adcf05127f40cec467346","body":{"detail":"The reopen route (POST .../reporter/reports/<tid>/reopen) accepts verified and resolved reports, and a comment no longer reopens one, but ReportView shows Still broken only inside {#if waiting} (a fix_proposed report) and no reply box on a resolved thread. A reporter whose confirmed fix regressed, or whose report was closed wontfix, can only file a new report.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"31182e30a64b70b64e6eead4f350c04f43797e14411e7751f4b34a003b05b6f7"},"suggested_fix":"Show Still broken on verified and resolved reports the reporter filed; this needs the overlay to know which reports are its own (see the concern on line 56).","summary":"The overlay offers no Still broken on a verified or resolved report the reporter filed","tags":["feedback","overlay","spec:6.3","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/ReportView.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:44:36.356908Z","id":"219389ac6a214d7fda981f3afe469daabbfac9c8b0f524e034bd4fb06ec7916c","body":{"detail":"Every author_kind reporter comment is labelled You, including another reporter's. Another reporter's fix_proposed report shows It's fixed and Still broken, which the server refuses with 404 not_found (check_verdict_in in crates/clax-store/src/queues.rs), shown as a raw message by failureText in web/overlay/src/model.ts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"268a49e99eaf6c07eb1fc105464c0972ac72bda0aa450d02f7207a888c392662"},"suggested_fix":"Mark reports mine: true on the reporter routes (the token's reporter_id), show verdicts only on those, label others' comments Another reporter, and map not_found in failureText.","summary":"Under reporters_see: all the overlay labels another reporter's comment You, and offers verdicts on others' reports that answer 404","tags":["feedback","overlay","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:36.495477Z","id":"e85e40c5bc12d315ae6355e37db8ae02c7d7de0c5c8f860be909cae73d7efe4d","body":{"detail":"The poll calls client.myReports() without a cursor and replaces the list with page.reports. A reporter with more reports than the server's page size never sees the older ones, and a reply on one of them does not show.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":364},"end":{"line":369},"content_hash":"71df012d61085aecd4487f7d2c674fb173dd7c961f5250e67cf8684ce38882c7"},"suggested_fix":"Follow next on demand (a Show more button at the list's end), keeping the polled first page merged with the loaded tail by report ID.","summary":"Your reports shows only the first page of myReports; the cursor (next) is never followed","supersedes":"190a6f5dae8aa08534e480442968a7704eb4d175a44fc2e362992b96e36e34c8","tags":["overlay","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:36.594289Z","id":"ca0347842021692e03afcc73ae2e0be1ed5fe513dc6c71c17377db2db9976475","body":{"detail":"The overlay runs in the page's own world (unlike the extension's, web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts, which uses closed roots and an extension-page composer). It is open so Playwright can reach it in web/e2e. The page is the deployer's own, which already holds the reporter's session and the auth callback, and the reporter's Ed25519 key is non-extractable (web/sdk/src/sign.ts), so a closed root would add little; a third-party script on that page can read typed text either way.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"2506fc8ee180769cea1d77c3ed518fa3b35075d43268bba807a3dbe05810e5b5"},"summary":"The overlay's shadow root is open, so the page's scripts can read and drive its composer","supersedes":"127bf81715ef8f5d14c554208c1c67349f64c35523a99462db5f8bcedd94e622","tags":["overlay","security","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:24:03.522165Z","id":"852932cc30ca4760c46a869d0a7f7fc10e35878056a05d0d229965d184461c7a","body":{"detail":"Overlay.svelte makes its picker (overlay/src/picker.ts commentPicker, which appends a CommentMode host <clax-overlay> to <html>, bridge/src/comment-mode.ts:170-179) while the component initialises, and destroys it from onDestroy. Svelte 5 registers an onDestroy teardown through an effect, which runs only once effects flush. When a page calls overlay(...) and then close() on its handle before the next task, unmount finds no teardown: the overlay's own host is removed (main.ts close) but the picker's host and its listeners stay. Seen with the SDK package's bundle (web/sdk/package.test.ts, which waits a task before close for this reason): without the wait, two <clax-overlay> elements are in the page after overlay() and one after close().","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"e99294377d9d8512e61895e922c0f2e1ed6cd39894a2fe8b7f5054392fdca031"},"suggested_fix":"Make the picker in an $effect (or onMount) that returns its destroy, so it exists only once its teardown does; or destroy it in main.ts close() as well as in onDestroy.","summary":"close() in the same task as overlay() leaves comment mode's <clax-overlay> host in the page","tags":["session:claude-code:369633e5-7e93-4e72-b6c2-aedba48817c5"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:06:45.501876Z","id":"983302d7c9d1ea47cedbf6caa81671d6638e2b574e378089e3c5ae97e79c6b32","body":{"detail":"With /_clax/overlay.js a page calls Clax.overlay once. Through @empathic/clax-sdk/overlay an app calls overlay() in a useEffect and close() in its cleanup; React's StrictMode runs one extra setup, cleanup and setup cycle in development (https://react.dev/reference/react/StrictMode), within the same commit, so every such app in development leaves a <clax-overlay> picker host and its listeners behind. web/sdk/package.test.ts:99-101 waits a task before close() to step around this.","kind":"comment","references":"852932cc30ca4760c46a869d0a7f7fc10e35878056a05d0d229965d184461c7a","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"e99294377d9d8512e61895e922c0f2e1ed6cd39894a2fe8b7f5054392fdca031"},"summary":"As an npm import this path is the common case, not an edge: a React app in StrictMode closes the overlay in the task that opened it","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:00.339624Z","id":"1e11d25a799d5bf7410207e93a47422841c0e3e7ae539e95d69be736326a57c4","body":{"detail":"https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect (Caveats): 'When Strict Mode is on, React will run one extra development-only setup+cleanup cycle before the first real setup'; Troubleshooting: 'runs setup+cleanup one extra time immediately after component mounts'. https://react.dev/reference/react/StrictMode: development only. React's source, packages/react-reconciler/src/ReactFiberWorkLoop.js at v19.1.0, flushPassiveEffectsImpl calls commitPassiveMountEffects (line 4131) and then, in the same function, `if (__DEV__) commitDoubleInvokeEffectsInDEV(root, true)` (line 4144), so the first setup and the extra cleanup run in one task with no flush of Svelte's effects between. web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte:43-44 makes the picker at init and destroys it in onDestroy; web/overlay/src/main.ts:54-70 mounts with no flushSync and close() calls unmount; web/sdk/package.test.ts:99-101 waits a setTimeout(0) before close(). Scope: development builds only (production runs one setup), so an app in StrictMode leaks one picker host per mount in development.","kind":"comment","references":"983302d7c9d1ea47cedbf6caa81671d6638e2b574e378089e3c5ae97e79c6b32","summary":"confirmed: StrictMode's extra setup/cleanup runs synchronously in the same passive-effects flush, so overlay() then close() land in one task","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:36:12.513299Z","id":"74f59ca65c6c293f1cb549beb47a0f018c8c075de8f56d4f3415dcf6ea9359cb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:df2fbede","summary":"The picker is now made in onMount, which returns its destroy, so an overlay unmounted before its effects ran never makes it. web/overlay/src/main.test.ts 'leaves nothing in the page when closed in the task that started it' (overlay(opts).close(), no wait) failed before the change ('expected <clax-overlay></clax-overlay> to have a length of +0 but got 1') and passes after under //web:unit; web/sdk/package.test.ts no longer waits a setTimeout(0) before close() and //web:sdk_package passes.","supersedes":"852932cc30ca4760c46a869d0a7f7fc10e35878056a05d0d229965d184461c7a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T16:20:15.903438Z","id":"36bf5c4083363f87033e3da3daa7ff46ec3ddb49c67d45b635ab26df92094e73","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ed5372a5a407b8bff945d644f1287a3c9056d8ea","summary":"The picker is now made in onMount, which returns its destroy, so an overlay unmounted before its effects ran never makes it. web/overlay/src/main.test.ts 'leaves nothing in the page when closed in the task that started it' (overlay(opts).close(), no wait) failed before the change ('expected <clax-overlay></clax-overlay> to have a length of +0 but got 1') and passes after under //web:unit; web/sdk/package.test.ts no longer waits a setTimeout(0) before close() and //web:sdk_package passes.","supersedes":"74f59ca65c6c293f1cb549beb47a0f018c8c075de8f56d4f3415dcf6ea9359cb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T16:31:03.546433Z","id":"35573897874d3a3e93f63774f0edba66c2206f03180cc8d86e7103593c2178c3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c0ffe1c9897891371159c1f79bdbb93c3936099e","summary":"The picker is now made in onMount, which returns its destroy, so an overlay unmounted before its effects ran never makes it. web/overlay/src/main.test.ts 'leaves nothing in the page when closed in the task that started it' (overlay(opts).close(), no wait) failed before the change ('expected <clax-overlay></clax-overlay> to have a length of +0 but got 1') and passes after under //web:unit; web/sdk/package.test.ts no longer waits a setTimeout(0) before close() and //web:sdk_package passes.","supersedes":"36bf5c4083363f87033e3da3daa7ff46ec3ddb49c67d45b635ab26df92094e73","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T03:21:52.527982Z","id":"7666e9019e34c81204fcd16fcd700d1a17058589128c08623167824d974531c2","body":{"detail":"The poll calls client.myReports() without a cursor and replaces the list with page.reports. A reporter with more reports than the server's page size never sees the older ones, and a reply on one of them does not show.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored after merge c20bac570 moved the lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":371},"end":{"line":376},"content_hash":"71df012d61085aecd4487f7d2c674fb173dd7c961f5250e67cf8684ce38882c7"},"suggested_fix":"Follow next on demand (a Show more button at the list's end), keeping the polled first page merged with the loaded tail by report ID.","summary":"Your reports shows only the first page of myReports; the cursor (next) is never followed","supersedes":"e85e40c5bc12d315ae6355e37db8ae02c7d7de0c5c8f860be909cae73d7efe4d","tags":["overlay","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T03:21:53.115858Z","id":"59b4f5c3500a5918c24fd51d747e192a1fd5ab0b265d8931060fab73c3a6ce52","body":{"detail":"The overlay runs in the page's own world (unlike the extension's, web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts, which uses closed roots and an extension-page composer). It is open so Playwright can reach it in web/e2e. The page is the deployer's own, which already holds the reporter's session and the auth callback, and the reporter's Ed25519 key is non-extractable (web/sdk/src/sign.ts), so a closed root would add little; a third-party script on that page can read typed text either way.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored after merge c20bac570 moved the lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"2506fc8ee180769cea1d77c3ed518fa3b35075d43268bba807a3dbe05810e5b5"},"summary":"The overlay's shadow root is open, so the page's scripts can read and drive its composer","supersedes":"ca0347842021692e03afcc73ae2e0be1ed5fe513dc6c71c17377db2db9976475","tags":["overlay","security","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T03:21:55.338828Z","id":"362895ccb9504a4948a959a551ea1b751281552c425b85f06a8c7c5077a9a220","body":{"detail":"Main's change (picker made in onMount, so an overlay closed before its effects ran leaves no comment mode in the page) and the feedback loop's mode bar now meet: choose() and setPicking() call picker?.set/areasOnly/keyboard, which do nothing while picker is null. Svelte 5's mount runs no effects synchronously, so a host with launcher: false that calls the handle's report() in the same task as overlay() gets the mode bar without picking. web/overlay tests pass; no test calls report() before a flush.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"3024ff9d6bff7b63c19b9c87b045fa5eca7137af6da53ea5e61fe622788341f5"},"summary":"The picker is made in onMount, so report() or the mode bar used before the overlay's effects first run picks nothing","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:56:47.896470Z","id":"51c631fe70a1f772953ac1f5ca062f0ffaa8b6bc0db740bf022b45568330cb4b","body":{"detail":"web/overlay/src/options.ts:1-2 says the overlay's public types (main.ts) \"reach the SDK's reporter types and nothing of the bridge\". But main.ts imports `type Mode` from ./capture and `CONTEXT_TIMEOUT_MS` from ./model (lines 23-24) and re-exports both (lines 30-31). build-sdk.mjs's declaration emit then ships every declaration they reach under types/overlay/src and types/bridge/src, including the bridge's frame protocol and model.ts's imports of SDK types the public API never names. Any app type-checking without skipLibCheck checks all of them, so an edit to web/bridge made for the shell, or renaming an SDK type the overlay uses internally, can break type-checking of an installed package.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"e21ef64a42526928153361451283afef1979fc342d79bd709925db6e56d0e851"},"suggested_fix":"Move `Mode` (\"element\" | \"area\" | \"screen\") and `CONTEXT_TIMEOUT_MS` into web/overlay/src/options.ts and import them from there in capture.ts and model.ts, so main.d.ts reaches only options.d.ts and the SDK's types. Add a check to web/sdk/package.test.ts that types/overlay holds just main.d.ts and options.d.ts.","summary":"The ./overlay entry's published declarations reach model.ts, capture.ts, picker.ts and web/bridge modules through `Mode` and `CONTEXT_TIMEOUT_MS`, against what options.ts:1-2 says the public types reach","tags":["review","review:pr45-client-split","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:42:07.324446Z","id":"3d6f4714a11ec48f9c96d153766c03c387834973c47ed0d323c57ae6e3805be0","body":{"detail":"Main's change (picker made in onMount, so an overlay closed before its effects ran leaves no comment mode in the page) and the feedback loop's mode bar now meet: choose() and setPicking() call picker?.set/areasOnly/keyboard, which do nothing while picker is null. Svelte 5's mount runs no effects synchronously, so a host with launcher: false that calls the handle's report() in the same task as overlay() gets the mode bar without picking. web/overlay tests pass; no test calls report() before a flush.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"3024ff9d6bff7b63c19b9c87b045fa5eca7137af6da53ea5e61fe622788341f5"},"summary":"The picker is made in onMount, so report() or the mode bar used before the overlay's effects first run picks nothing","supersedes":"362895ccb9504a4948a959a551ea1b751281552c425b85f06a8c7c5077a9a220","tags":["session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:42:07.454576Z","id":"ba85d80e6e5bd807fb64d27b24fe26d3452254f95546a5ec0ec02f58c92d8ca5","body":{"detail":"The poll calls client.myReports() without a cursor and replaces the list with page.reports. A reporter with more reports than the server's page size never sees the older ones, and a reply on one of them does not show.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored after merge c20bac570 moved the lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":372},"end":{"line":377},"content_hash":"71df012d61085aecd4487f7d2c674fb173dd7c961f5250e67cf8684ce38882c7"},"suggested_fix":"Follow next on demand (a Show more button at the list's end), keeping the polled first page merged with the loaded tail by report ID.","summary":"Your reports shows only the first page of myReports; the cursor (next) is never followed","supersedes":"7666e9019e34c81204fcd16fcd700d1a17058589128c08623167824d974531c2","tags":["overlay","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:42:07.584230Z","id":"d32c9b4076a72af83ca17f94bdfcaea9117fd1374d9227e9136b5e868115b4be","body":{"detail":"The overlay runs in the page's own world (unlike the extension's, web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts, which uses closed roots and an extension-page composer). It is open so Playwright can reach it in web/e2e. The page is the deployer's own, which already holds the reporter's session and the auth callback, and the reporter's Ed25519 key is non-extractable (web/sdk/src/sign.ts), so a closed root would add little; a third-party script on that page can read typed text either way.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored after merge c20bac570 moved the lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"2506fc8ee180769cea1d77c3ed518fa3b35075d43268bba807a3dbe05810e5b5"},"summary":"The overlay's shadow root is open, so the page's scripts can read and drive its composer","supersedes":"59b4f5c3500a5918c24fd51d747e192a1fd5ab0b265d8931060fab73c3a6ce52","tags":["overlay","security","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:42:07.782283Z","id":"a078c0a6bcf4086a9a01a21c0d837713f6ed6f7af77504785cd81c596e8c180a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:196a66457","summary":"Mode and CONTEXT_TIMEOUT_MS now live in web/overlay/src/options.ts; main.ts, capture.ts, model.ts, ModeBar.svelte and Overlay.svelte import them from there, so the built types/overlay holds only src/main.d.ts and src/options.d.ts and types/bridge is gone. web/sdk/package.test.ts \"keeps the overlay entry's declarations to its public interface\" checks it; //web:sdk_package passes (bazelisk test --lockfile_mode=error //web/... //scripts/...: 40 tests pass).","supersedes":"51c631fe70a1f772953ac1f5ca062f0ffaa8b6bc0db740bf022b45568330cb4b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:43:12.306316Z","id":"d44ab07fb15f84dbef2ce49ce1bdb05a7d4becdbace464178fed531a0675339d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d254a64870559e46670618bd31466e7737ff4be5","summary":"Mode and CONTEXT_TIMEOUT_MS now live in web/overlay/src/options.ts; main.ts, capture.ts, model.ts, ModeBar.svelte and Overlay.svelte import them from there, so the built types/overlay holds only src/main.d.ts and src/options.d.ts and types/bridge is gone. web/sdk/package.test.ts \"keeps the overlay entry's declarations to its public interface\" checks it; //web:sdk_package passes (bazelisk test --lockfile_mode=error //web/... //scripts/...: 40 tests pass).","supersedes":"a078c0a6bcf4086a9a01a21c0d837713f6ed6f7af77504785cd81c596e8c180a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:43.506467Z","id":"d14a16cfc203e32133325ea862dd1e2ca9af1dd737858218ab0eec9d9219a879","body":{"detail":"The overlay runs in the page's own world (unlike the extension's, web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts, which uses closed roots and an extension-page composer). It is open so Playwright can reach it in web/e2e. The page is the deployer's own, which already holds the reporter's session and the auth callback, and the reporter's Ed25519 key is non-extractable (web/sdk/src/sign.ts), so a closed root would add little; a third-party script on that page can read typed text either way.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored after merge c20bac570 moved the lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":134},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"2506fc8ee180769cea1d77c3ed518fa3b35075d43268bba807a3dbe05810e5b5"},"summary":"The overlay's shadow root is open, so the page's scripts can read and drive its composer","supersedes":"d32c9b4076a72af83ca17f94bdfcaea9117fd1374d9227e9136b5e868115b4be","tags":["overlay","security","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T17:30:00.998633Z","id":"3d84e81ab5b4a1c37a30e18576f7de3d4f9920450a7b34557d54e0a33113ccbe","body":{"detail":"Without onShowReports, the launcher's \"Your reports\" opens the panel on the report the badge last rose for (waitingId, set by BadgeWatch's rose hook at the badge section of Overlay.svelte). With onShowReports, launcherReports calls it with no report, and waitingId stays for the panel's next opening (showReports()). The badge gives report IDs, not Reports, so carrying it means fetching the report first or widening the hook's argument to an ID; the host's own page can order waiting reports first from myReports() instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":403},"end":{"line":408},"content_hash":"d064836cfdcac15aaef770c33a41dc1044e2737b734e9802dc92238e1bf87025"},"summary":"The launcher's onShowReports call could carry the report the badge newly says is waiting","tags":["revisit:a host asks to open its page on the report waiting on the reporter","session:claude-code:20fc3cee-59da-423a-865b-f12fb53bd8ad"]}}
